From 0ff1d15b0d80aedd455a956cef89fcb327475b08 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rohit Thanvi <rohit@nyaya-ai.local>
Date: Tue, 30 Jun 2026 06:01:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] Remove nested duplicate folder; fix retrieval and
 ingestion bugs

- Remove accidental nested Nyaya/Nyaya/ duplicate directory
- BM25: fix synonym expansion (was AND-ing IPC/BNS synonyms via
  websearch_to_tsquery, silently zeroing recall); now OR's correctly
- BM25: normalize PG/ES scores before merging tiers so unbounded ES
  scores don't silently dominate PG ts_rank_cd scores
- BM25: drop unused ts_headline computation (wasted CPU per query)
- Reranker: normalize RRF hybrid_score before blending with sigmoid
  rerank_score (previously hybrid contributed ~0% due to scale mismatch)
- Vector: make Qdrant upsert wait configurable, default False for
  bulk ingestion throughput
- Pipeline: remove dead no-op nested-transaction block
- Embeddings: fix embed_batch_sync using wrong settings field
  (ingest_batch_size instead of batch_size) for Celery workers
- Embeddings: add lock around model loading to prevent concurrent
  double-load race
- Ingestion: ingest_directory now actually uses bounded concurrency
  (parser_concurrency was defined in settings but never wired up;
  was fully sequential for thousands of documents)
- Ingestion: remove dead no-op UPDATE chunks SET chunk_type=chunk_type
- Migration: drop redundant per-row tsvector trigger (app already
  computes it explicitly on insert; trigger fought batched-insert perf)
- Chunker: wire up page_map so chunks get real page_number instead
  of always None (page_map was already built by the parser and
  unused)
