From 4349ed0949d3dcfcd14bb6b6ad4e672f765e65f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rohit Thanvi <rohit@nyaya-ai.local>
Date: Tue, 30 Jun 2026 16:37:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] Fix auth 422/307/client-crash bugs, calibrate confidence
 scoring
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Auth/HTTP bugs:
- Six routes (chat, documents, drafting, health, search, upload) were
  declared with a trailing slash while the frontend calls them without
  one. redirect_slashes=False (already set) turned this into silent
  404s instead of 307 redirects, but the actual mismatch was never
  fixed. Routes now match what the frontend sends exactly.
- FastAPI 422 validation errors return detail as an ARRAY of
  {loc, msg, type} objects, not a string. Five frontend call sites
  (login/register, judgments, search, upload, drafting) were doing
  toast.error(err.response.data.detail) directly — passing that array
  straight into toast.error(), which is the likely cause of the
  reported client-side exception on registration. Added a shared
  getErrorMessage() helper that safely flattens any FastAPI error
  shape into a readable string, used everywhere.
- Added client-side password length validation (8 char minimum) on
  the register form so the most common 422 trigger is caught before
  the request even fires, with a clear inline hint.

Confidence scoring (backend/agents/assembly/agent.py):
- Fixed double-penalization: hallucination flags were lowering
  verify_ratio's denominator AND being subtracted again via a
  separate penalty term, double-counting the same signal.
- Fixed unrealistic 0.7 'moderate confidence' baseline for answers
  with zero verifiable citations — replaced with 0.35, since zero
  checkable claims is a low-confidence signal for a legal research
  tool, not a neutral one.
- Added evidence breadth scaling (1 retrieved chunk now scores lower
  than 3+, even if that one chunk had a high score) and source
  diversity (chunks from multiple independent documents score higher
  than the same number of chunks from one document).
- Hallucinated/stripped claims now apply a hard confidence CEILING
  rather than an additive penalty, since catching and removing a
  hallucination means the underlying generation had a real defect
  regardless of how clean the surviving claims look.
- Added confidence_breakdown to LegalResponse (band, retrieval
  quality, source diversity, verification ratio, chunk/claim counts)
  so confidence is never an opaque number — surfaced in both backend
  model and frontend TypeScript types.
