From 878a334041e08cc2128c7b49b0adc9178c80ae28 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rohit Thanvi <rohit@nyaya-ai.local>
Date: Wed, 1 Jul 2026 05:07:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] Fix all auth bugs: cookie path/secure/scope, register
 INSERT, stale store, refresh loop
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Frontend (frontend/lib/api.ts):
- secure:true on cookies breaks all auth on localhost HTTP — the browser
  silently drops cookies marked secure on non-HTTPS origins. Added
  IS_SECURE flag (true only when protocol is https:) and shared
  COOKIE_OPTIONS with path:'/' and environment-aware secure flag.
- All Cookies.set calls were missing path:'/' — cookies set at
  /auth/login were scoped to that path, invisible to /dashboard,
  /search, etc., so every subsequent authenticated request got 401.
- All Cookies.remove calls were missing path:'/' — without the same
  scope used at set-time, remove() silently does nothing. Stale tokens
  stayed in the browser and the 401 interceptor looped indefinitely.
- Added expires (1 day access, 30 day refresh) to prevent session-only
  cookies being discarded on every browser close.
- Hardened 401 interceptor: no longer attempts refresh for /auth/*
  routes (hitting /auth/login with a 401 was recursively trying to
  refresh, not a refresh-worthy scenario). Now clears Zustand store
  alongside cookies when forcing redirect.

Frontend (frontend/components/auth/AuthGuard.tsx):
- Guard now rejects empty-string tokens (possible if a secure cookie
  was set but silently dropped, leaving a name-only cookie with no value).

Frontend (frontend/lib/store.ts):
- useAuthStore.persist saves isAuthenticated:true to localStorage.
  If both JWT cookies expire while the browser is closed, the next
  session finds isAuthenticated:true in the store but no cookies,
  causing a flash of authenticated UI before the first 401 fires.
  Added syncWithCookies() action (called on AppLayout mount) that
  wipes persisted auth state if no access_token cookie is present.

Frontend (frontend/components/layout/AppLayout.tsx):
- Call syncWithCookies() on mount to immediately correct stale store.

Frontend (frontend/app/auth/login/page.tsx):
- Added client-side min-length=8 password validation for register
  mode with an inline hint, preventing the most common 422 trigger.

Backend (backend/api/routes/auth.py):
- Register INSERT now provides explicit user_id (uuid4()) and
  is_active=True rather than relying on DB defaults — if uuid-ossp
  extension isn't loaded, the DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4() call fails
  with a cryptic DB error and the user never gets created.
- Email normalized to lowercase+strip on both register and login so
  a user who registered with 'User@Email.com' can log in with
  'user@email.com'.
- Added empty email/password check on login before hitting bcrypt.

Backend (backend/models/domain.py):
- UserLogin now has min_length validators to reject blank form submits
  at the Pydantic layer before touching the database.
